  id: Left_Lobe
  partName: Left Lobe
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'The left lobe of the liver, though smaller than the right, is an active metabolic
    zone responsible for detoxification, glycogen storage, and protein synthesis.
    It receives blood from both the portal vein and the hepatic artery, ensuring
    a steady supply of nutrients for processing. '
  - This lobe contributes to bile secretion and plays an important role in filtering
    blood before it returns to systemic circulation. Its function complements the
    right lobe, ensuring balanced hepatic workload and maintaining efficient overall
    liver performance.
